// Granted/revoked by Heroes/Zara/VoidDamageWavesSkillAction - read by
// SpawnAlternatingAreaEffectData.ApplyVoidUpgrade off the speaker's own owner, appending
// RiftMarkEffect into the first open DamageEffects slot at spawn. Silently does nothing if
// DamageEffects already fills all 4 slots. Migrated from PoisonDamageWavesUpgrade once Poison was
// removed, then from a Void-status grant to a Rift Mark grant once Void was promoted to a real
// damage element - see docs/elemental-reactions.md. The component/skill keep their historical
// "VoidDamageWaves" name (same precedent as the earlier Poison->Void migration); only the effect it
// grants changed - it marks whatever it pulses over with a Rift Mark stack, priming it for whichever
// element (this Zara's own, or a teammate's) lands next.
component VoidDamageWavesUpgrade
{
    AssetRef<HitEffectData> RiftMarkEffect;
}
